*.spl
*.fls
*.fdb_latexmk
# main.abs is written by the cas class on every compile (it extracts the
# abstract). It had been committed instead, so every build produced a
# spurious tracked diff.
*.abs
build.log

# main.pdf is NOT ignored, deliberately. It was, and that is why three
# submissions reached the referee without a compiled manuscript even though
# SUBMISSION_FILES.md listed it: a package assembled from the repository
# silently omitted the one file the rule excluded. The guide requires
# editable sources AND a compiled PDF; paper/check_submission.py now fails
# if the PDF is absent or older than the sources it was built from.
